Implementation of finding the enclosing branch:

```rust
fn branch_body<'a>(src: &'a str, header: &str) -> Option<&'a str> {
    let start = src.find(header)? + header.len();
    let mut depth = 1usize;
    for (i, ch) in src[start..].char_indices() {
        match ch {
            '{' => depth += 1,
            '}' => {
                depth -= 1;
                if depth == 0 {
                    return Some(&src[start..start + i]);
                }
            }
            _ => {}
        }
    }
    None
}
```

Caveat: braces inside string literals would break it — but the branch body contains `system_prompt.push_str("\n\n# Project Instructions\n\n");` which has no braces. Fine, and if it broke, the guard goes red loudly rather than silently passing. Actually, a broken brace match could return None → I'd panic with a message. It's a weak guard; fine. But better to state the limit.

